    "Women with STEMI had a higher risk of failure to receive reperfusion therapy due to delays and risks associated with antithrombotic therapy. Disparities in treatment among racial and ethnic minorities showed improvement over time. Patients with diabetes mellitus face higher risks post-STEMI, often associated with longer hospital stays and worse outcomes. Management should focus on glycemic control and account for impaired renal function in the elderly to improve outcomes. Analysis from various registries emphasizes the need for guideline-recommended interventions to lessen disparities and improve care, particularly in patients with chronic kidney disease.": []
